---
import LegalLayout from "../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { site, partners } from "../../data/site";
---

<LegalLayout title="Data Processing Addendum (Summary)">
  <p>
    This page summarizes our data processing practices for business customers. A full Data Processing Addendum (DPA) is available on request
    by contacting <a href={`mailto:${site.emails.legal}`}>{site.emails.legal}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="roles">Roles</h2>
  <p>
    For customer-provided training data, the customer is typically the <strong>data controller</strong> and Prime AI Company acts as a{" "}
    <strong>data processor</strong>, processing data only on documented instructions in the statement of work.
  </p>

  <h2 id="subprocessors">Subprocessors</h2>
  <p>We may use vetted subprocessors for compute and storage, including:</p>
  <ul>
    {partners.slice(0, 4).map((p) => (
      <li>{p.name}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p>We will notify customers of material subprocessor changes where contractually required.</p>

  <h2 id="security">Security measures</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Encryption in transit (TLS) for data transfer.</li>
    <li>Role-based access to training environments.</li>
    <li>Customer-VPC or isolated cloud accounts where contracted.</li>
    <li>Deletion or return of data per SOW after project completion.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="requests">Data subject requests</h2>
  <p>
    We assist controllers with reasonable requests to access, correct, or delete personal data in training sets, subject to technical
    constraints and legal holds.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Full DPA</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.emails.legal}`}>{site.emails.legal}</a> for a countersigned DPA.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
